      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update airflow to 3.3.1-2 or later.",
      "status_notes": "sqlparse 0.6.0 fixes the quadratic CPU use in ReindentFilter._get_offset() by measuring the current line backwards from the token (GHSA-cfqr-cjx5-5jcm, fix commit https://github.com/andialbrecht/sqlparse/commit/a51df6d9e2d31b44be9adb6bc8732517db6bf96b, release https://github.com/andialbrecht/sqlparse/releases/tag/0.6.0). airflow bundles sqlparse in its Python environment under /usr/lib/airflow. Each of the 110 airflow packages published for Debian 13 in the DHI Debian repository (3.3.0-0 to 3.4.0-14, amd64 and arm64) was placed by what it installs, read from the package's own file list and md5sums: 3.3.0-0 to 3.3.0-3, 3.3.1-0 and 3.3.1-1 install sqlparse 0.5.5 and are affected; 3.3.1-2 to 3.3.2-19 install sqlparse 0.6.0 and 3.4.0-0 to 3.4.0-14 install 0.6.1. Each package's file list has a single sqlparse module directory. In the unpacked 3.3.1-2 package, sqlparse/filters/reindent.py defines _current_line_len and no longer has _flatten_up_to_token; the unpacked 3.3.1-1 package still has the old _flatten_up_to_token walk. Every build from 3.3.1-2 on, on both architectures, ships a reindent.py with the same md5 as 3.3.1-2's. 3.3.1-2 is the first published package with the fix."
    },
